#[doc("""
Kaikai values across the C boundary as `void *` userdata.

`retain_userdata` parks a private copy of a value behind a `Userdata` handle, which an
`extern "C"` import passes to C and an exported `extern "C" fn` receives
back; `take_userdata` reads a fresh copy of the value, `release_userdata` frees the parked one.
The handle keeps the copy alive for as long as C may call back, on any
thread. State belongs in actors: park the `Pid` of the owner and send it
messages from the callback.

`take_userdata[t]` trusts the caller about `t`: reading a handle at a type other than
the one it was retained at is undefined behaviour.
""")]

#[doc("A kaikai value parked for C; crosses the boundary as `void *`.")]
extern "C" pub opaque Userdata

#[doc("Parks a private copy of `v` and returns its handle.")]
extern "kai"("kai_ffi_retain") pub fn retain_userdata[t](v: t) : Userdata

#[doc("A fresh copy of the value parked behind `u`; the handle stays valid.")]
extern "kai"("kai_ffi_take") pub fn take_userdata[t](u: Userdata) : t

#[doc("Frees the value parked behind `u`; the handle must not be used afterwards.")]
extern "kai"("kai_ffi_release") pub fn release_userdata(u: Userdata) : Unit
